<title>USA: Texaco sets 30 pct capital spending rise.</title>
<headline>Texaco sets 30 pct capital spending rise.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc said Tuesday it plans a $4.5 billion 1997 capital and exploratory program which would be up more than 30 percent from a level of $3.4 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;The increase in 1997 spending will kick off our five-year capex program, with some $24.3 billion targeted between 1997 and 2001, an increase of nearly 60 percent over capital expenditures from the 1992 through 1996 period,&quot; the company said, reiterating the projection given to analysts in early December.  </p>
<p>Below is a table showing the functional and geographic breakdown for 1997 capital spending funds in billions of dollars:</p>
<p> Function	   U.S.  International  Worldwide   Percentage</p>
<p> Upstream	   $1.4	$1.5	    $2.9	   65%</p>
<p> Downstream	   .5	 1.0	     1.5	   33%</p>
<p> Other		 0.0	  .1		.1	    2%</p>
<p> Total		$1.9	$2.6	    $4.5</p>
<p> Percentage	   42%	 58%	    100%	  100%</p>
<p>((-- Jim Brumm 212-859-1710.))</p>
